# Derived, disposable, or personal to one machine. Nothing here is needed by
# anyone who clones this repo or contributes to it.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Test and build output
app/tests/_out/
build/
dist/
*.spec

# Runtime state, written by the app on the machine it runs on
app/logs/
app/recordings/
app/cache/
app/reports/

# Written by Doctor.cmd beside itself when it runs from source
doctor-report.txt

# Measured on ONE camera in ONE room. A fresh install measures its own; a
# borrowed calibration is worse than none, and `packaging/assemble.py`
# refuses to put either of these in a release.
app/config/settings.local.json
app/config/calibration.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HIS OWN MATERIAL. In the working tree, never in the repository.
#
# Copied in 2026-10-23 when development moved here, so the harness and the
# session hook work from this folder alone and nothing reaches back into
# C:\WORKSPACE\Laser.Shooting.App any more.
#
# His criterion decided every line of it: "we will not release the files that
# would not be needed by other people who decide to clone the repo and/or
# contribute to the repo." RULES.md and CLAUDE.md are the agreement between
# him and me -- "those are between me and you, people will not understand
# what that file is for". The specs under requirements/ are working documents
# that source comments cite. agent_reports/ is the session record. The two
# config files carry a calibration measured on HIS camera in HIS room and the
# sensitivity his own trigger pulls taught it: shipping them would hand a
# stranger a mapping for a monitor they do not own.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/RULES.md
/CLAUDE.md
/.claude/
/agent_reports/
/requirements/
/calib_backups/

# test output: test_ui_smoke renders the target screen here
/app/target_screen.png
